<Layout title="About Shayaan | Padel Coach in Nairobi" description="Meet Shayaan, a Nairobi-based padel player and coach helping players improve exclusively at Ace Padel, Aga Khan Sports Centre."><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Player first. Coach always.</p><h1>Meet Shayaan.</h1><p class="lead">A Nairobi-based padel player and approachable, serious coach focused on helping every level understand the game—not just hit another ball.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container resource-banner"><div class="prose"><h2>Why I coach</h2><p>I have played padel for three years and coached for the last year. What keeps me interested is how much the game rewards understanding: where you stand, what your partner needs and which shot creates the next opportunity.</p><p>I coach complete beginners, developing players, intermediate players and competitive players. My aim is to make improvement practical and visible through clear feedback, purposeful repetition and realistic match situations.</p><h2>Connected to Nairobi padel</h2><p>I am partnered with Ace Padel Kenya and coach exclusively at Ace Padel, Aga Khan Sports Centre. It is my coaching home—not a club I own—and the place where my sessions are delivered.</p><h2>Understand. Build. Compete.</h2><p>First we understand why a pattern or mistake happens. Then we build technique and movement that can be repeated. Finally, we test it when the score and pressure are real.</p><Button href={site.bookingUrl} variant="dark" external event="book_coaching_click">Train With Shayaan</Button></div><div class="image-slot" style="min-height:650px"><small>Shayaan action photography slot</small></div></div></section></Layout>
